---
description: Anti-patterns that must never appear in code. A checklist of "don'ts".
alwaysApply: true
---

# Anti-patterns to never commit

If you're about to do one of these, stop. Find another way, or ask Nikola.

## 1. God objects

A single file with > 500 lines of unrelated logic. Split it.

## 2. Magic numbers

```ts
// BAD
if (user.age > 18) { ... }
setTimeout(fn, 86400000)

// GOOD
const ADULT_AGE = 18
const ONE_DAY_MS = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000
if (user.age > ADULT_AGE) { ... }
setTimeout(fn, ONE_DAY_MS)
```

## 3. Copy-pasted logic

If the same block appears in 3 places, extract a function. If you can't easily name
the function, the abstraction is wrong — think again.

## 4. N+1 queries

```ts
// BAD
const claims = await repo.list()
for (const claim of claims) {
  claim.employee = await employeesRepo.findById(claim.employeeId)  // N+1!
}

// GOOD
const claims = await repo.listWithEmployees()  // single query with JOIN
```

## 5. Swallowed errors

```ts
// BAD
try { risky() } catch (e) {}

// BAD
try { risky() } catch (e) { console.log('oops') }

// GOOD
try { risky() } catch (e) {
  logger.error({ err: e, context: { ... } }, 'Failed to foo')
  throw new AppError(...) // or handle meaningfully
}
```

## 6. Mixing concerns

```ts
// BAD — controller doing DB, validation, business logic
app.post('/api/claim', async (c) => {
  const body = await c.req.json()
  if (!body.mrNumber) return c.json({ error: 'No MR' }, 400)
  const claim = await db.insert(...).values(body).returning()
  await db.insert(auditLog).values({ ... })
  sendEmail(...)
  return c.json(claim[0])
})

// GOOD — thin controller, logic in service
app.post('/api/claim',
  requirePermission('claims.create'),
  async (c) => {
    const input = EmotiveClaimCreateInput.parse(await c.req.json())
    const claim = await container.claimsService.create(input, c.get('user'))
    return c.json(claim, 201)
  }
)
```

## 7. `// TODO: fix later`

TODOs without an issue number or deadline rot forever. Rules:
- Every TODO links to a GitHub issue: `// TODO(#142): handle concurrent edits`
- Or includes a deadline: `// TODO(2026-05-01): remove compat shim`
- Or is removed

## 8. Implicit state

```ts
// BAD — module-level mutable state
let currentUser: User | null = null

export function setUser(u: User) { currentUser = u }
export function getUser() { return currentUser }

// GOOD — explicit context
export interface AuthContext { user: User | null }
export function createHandler(ctx: AuthContext) { ... }
```

Module-level mutable state makes tests unreliable and code hard to reason about.

## 9. Global singletons

```ts
// BAD
export const db = drizzle(new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL }))
// every file imports this; tests can't swap it
```

Use DI container (`apps/api/src/core/container.ts`).

## 10. Fat models

Putting business logic on domain "model" classes that also know about persistence.
Keep entities as plain data; logic lives in services.

## 11. `any` to silence errors

```ts
// BAD
const x: any = getThing()
x.someMethod()

// GOOD
const x = getThing() as unknown
if (isThingLike(x)) {
  x.someMethod()
}

// BEST
const x = ThingSchema.parse(getThing())
x.someMethod()
```

## 12. Nested ternaries

```ts
// BAD
const label = status === 'pending' ? 'U obradi' : status === 'accepted' ? 'Prihvaćeno' : status === 'rejected' ? 'Odbijeno' : 'Arhiva'

// GOOD
const LABELS = { pending: 'U obradi', accepted: 'Prihvaćeno', rejected: 'Odbijeno', archived: 'Arhiva' }
const label = LABELS[status]
```

## 13. Comments that duplicate code

```ts
// BAD
// Increment counter
counter++

// Return user
return user
```

Comment **why**, not **what**.

## 14. Commented-out code

Delete it. Git remembers.

## 15. "Util" dumping grounds

A file called `utils.ts` with 40 unrelated functions is a code smell. Split into
domain-named files: `date.ts`, `string.ts`, `normalize-name.ts`.

## 16. Premature abstraction

Don't create an abstract base class for a concept that only has one implementation.
Don't add interfaces everywhere "just in case". The `StorageService` interface is
justified because R2 is a real future implementation.

## 17. Over-mocking

```ts
// BAD
it('works', async () => {
  const mockRepo = { findById: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ id: '1' }) }
  const mockEvents = { emit: vi.fn() }
  const mockAudit = { log: vi.fn() }
  const service = new Service(mockRepo, mockEvents, mockAudit)
  // what are we even testing?
})

// GOOD — integration test with real deps
it('works', async () => {
  const ctx = await createTestContext()
  const claim = await ctx.container.claimsService.create(validInput, user)
  expect(claim.id).toBeDefined()
})
```

## 18. Timing-dependent tests

```ts
// BAD
await page.click('Save')
await page.waitForTimeout(2000)  // hope it's enough
expect(toast).toBeVisible()

// GOOD
await page.click('Save')
await expect(toast).toBeVisible({ timeout: 5000 })  // waits up to 5s, passes as soon as visible
```

## 19. Synchronous blocking in async context

```ts
// BAD
const file = fs.readFileSync('./config.json')

// GOOD
const file = await fs.promises.readFile('./config.json')
```

## 20. Re-fetching in loops

```ts
// BAD
for (const id of ids) {
  const item = await fetch(`/api/items/${id}`)
  // ...
}

// GOOD
const items = await fetch('/api/items/batch', { body: { ids } })
// or parallel:
const items = await Promise.all(ids.map(id => fetch(`/api/items/${id}`)))
```

## 21. Hardcoded URLs or paths

```ts
// BAD
fetch('https://api.mrengines.rs/users')
fetch('http://localhost:3000/users')

// GOOD — relative path (same-origin proxy) or configured base URL
fetch('/api/users')
```

## 22. String HTML in components

```tsx
// BAD
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: userContent }} />

// GOOD
<div>{userContent}</div>  // React escapes automatically
```

## 23. Direct DOM manipulation

```tsx
// BAD
useEffect(() => {
  document.querySelector('.my-input')?.focus()
}, [])

// GOOD
const inputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null)
useEffect(() => { inputRef.current?.focus() }, [])
return <input ref={inputRef} />
```

## 24. Prop drilling

```tsx
// BAD
<A user={user}>
  <B user={user}>
    <C user={user}>
      <D user={user} />
    </C>
  </B>
</A>
```

Use a context or composition. But don't over-context either; 1–2 levels of drilling is fine.

## 25. useEffect for derived state

```ts
// BAD
const [fullName, setFullName] = useState('')
useEffect(() => { setFullName(`${first} ${last}`) }, [first, last])

// GOOD
const fullName = `${first} ${last}`
```

## 26. Fetching in useEffect

```ts
// BAD
useEffect(() => { fetch('/api/foo').then(r => r.json()).then(setData) }, [])

// GOOD
const { data } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['foo'], queryFn: () => fetchFoo() })
```

## 27. Reacting to render state

```tsx
// BAD — causes render loop
if (user) {
  setSomething(user.name)
}
```

## 28. "Helper" types that are really just `Record<string, any>`

Type safety dies here. Model your data properly.

## 29. Disabling eslint inline without reason

```ts
// BAD
// eslint-disable-next-line
doSomething()

// GOOD — with explanation and issue
// eslint-disable-next-line no-console -- we need console in this CLI script
console.log('...')
```

## 30. Reaching into internals

```ts
// BAD
import { _internal } from '@some/library'

// GOOD — respect public API
```

## 31. Forgetting the loading state

```tsx
// BAD
{data && <Items data={data} />}

// GOOD
{isLoading ? <Skeleton /> : error ? <ErrorState /> : data ? <Items data={data} /> : <EmptyState />}
```

## 32. console.log left in code

- `console.log` banned in production code (ESLint)
- Use `logger.debug` / `logger.info` via pino
- In React dev mode: `console.log` for debugging OK, but never committed

## 33. Reliance on exceptions for flow control

```ts
// BAD
try { parse(input) } catch (e) { return 'failed' }

// GOOD
const parsed = safeParse(input)
if (!parsed.success) return 'failed'
```

Use Zod's `safeParse` for expected failures. Throw for exceptional cases.

## 34. Boolean params (trap)

```ts
// BAD
function fetchClaims(all, includeDeleted, paginated) { ... }
fetchClaims(true, false, true)  // unreadable

// GOOD
function fetchClaims(opts: { scope: 'all' | 'mine'; includeDeleted?: boolean; pagination?: Pagination })
fetchClaims({ scope: 'all', pagination: { page: 1, pageSize: 20 } })
```

## 35. "Just use a Map"

`{}` is not `Map`. For dictionaries with dynamic keys, use `Map` to get iteration, size, and avoid prototype pitfalls.

## 36. Re-inventing libraries

Don't write a date formatter when `date-fns` works. Don't write a CSV parser when `papaparse` works. Don't write your own UUID generator.

## 37. Race conditions in React

```ts
// BAD
const [data, setData] = useState()
useEffect(() => {
  fetch().then(setData)  // stale data if user changes filter mid-flight
}, [filter])

// GOOD — use TanStack Query which cancels stale queries
```

## 38. Multiple sources of truth

If the same data is in `useState` and in a query cache, they'll diverge. Pick one.

## 39. Unbounded caches

Cache without eviction = memory leak. Always LRU or TTL.

## 40. Commit messages that say "fix"

```
git log:
  fix
  wip
  stuff
  oops
```

Useless. Follow conventional commits (see coding style rule).

---

If you're unsure whether something is an anti-pattern, ask Nikola before committing.
It's cheaper to rewrite a draft than to untangle a habit that spread across 20 files.
